  "provenance": {
    "detail": "val-match-v1 requires a Riot production key. Matches here are generated by an in-repo simulator that emits payloads in the documented val-match-v1 shape, grounded in real agent and map UUIDs fetched live from val-content-v1. Nothing is scraped and no unofficial API is used. Every module downstream of the match adapter is source-agnostic, so live data swaps in with no code change.",
    "note": "Simulated data conforming to the val-match-v1 schema \u2014 production key application pending",
    "proxy_note": "Momentum index, not a calibrated win probability: a bounded logistic over score state and round spend differential. It ranks rounds against each other within one match and says nothing about the odds of winning.",
    "sim_approx_note": "Kill share stands in for trade efficiency: the simulator emits no death timestamps, so real trade windows cannot be detected."
  },
